WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:06.980
The Trade Board is where pilots in your seat post trips they'd trade and answer each other's offers —

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:18.307
this one's a clearly marked example. Nothing here is a real trade: it's for finding each other, and real trades still go through FedEx's own process after bidding closes.

00:00:18.307 --> 00:00:25.437
Once you confirm what you hold, Line Select can also suggest trades that leave everyone on them better off.

00:00:26.395 --> 00:00:29.321
Your Inbox collects anything waiting on you.

00:00:29.321 --> 00:00:35.972
The board opens for your domicile, aircraft and seat once enough pilots there are using Line Select.

00:00:36.672 --> 00:00:45.343
A few last things. The Appearance menu switches between light and dark, and Night mode turns everything red to protect your night vision.

00:00:45.343 --> 00:00:47.938
"What's new" shows what's changed lately.

00:00:47.938 --> 00:00:53.951
And if anything's broken or confusing, "Send feedback" goes straight to the person building it.

00:00:55.291 --> 00:01:00.595
That's Line Select. Load your pack, tell it how you fly, and bid with confidence.

